.home {
  /* The artwork carries its own dark base and its own contrast, so the gradient
     only fades the foot of the hero into the page below it. Dimming the whole
     thing the way the photograph needed would crush the light out of it.

     Sized to one viewport at the top rather than `cover`, because `.home` is
     the whole search page and not just the hero: under `cover` the image grew
     with the results list, so a 16:9 canvas was blown up to twice the page
     width and its arcs ran across the filters and the result cards. One
     viewport tall is the region this art is actually for; below it the page is
     flat. `preserveAspectRatio="slice"` in the file means this crops rather
     than stretches. */
  background-image: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(13, 12, 20, 0) 0%, rgba(13, 12, 20, 0.55) 62%, #0d0c14 100%), url('/img/hero-routes.svg');
  background-size: 100% 100vh;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  background-position: top center;
  background-color: #0d0c14;
}

